@startuml run-states
' Revision (2026-10-13): accepted architecture-review findings (2026-10-13); design only.
' Workspace revision: accepted architecture-review findings (2026-10-13); design only.
title M-DP2: execution run/1 states, service slices (draft; one-shot intake gated)
state "accepted" as Accepted
state "queued (later capability)" as Queued
state "starting" as Starting
state "running" as Running
state "stopping" as Stopping
state "cleaning" as Cleaning
state "Terminal run state\ndone | failed | cancelled | expired" as Terminal
[*] --> Accepted : dispatcher accepts immutable input
Accepted --> Queued : later queue capability: temporary capacity closure
Accepted --> Starting : recorded class + host matrix + machine-selected exec body pin + authority + capacity admitted; fresh revocation.check(start); execution claim
Queued --> Starting : authority/window/quota + all gates rechecked; fresh revocation.check(dequeue)
Queued --> Queued : temporary closure / operator drain park
Starting --> Running : supervisor registered; launcher receipt recorded
Starting --> Stopping : cancel during/after launch; wait for receipt or refusal
Running --> Stopping : exit / explicit stop (cancel / authorised host_stop) / operator action / incident hard stop
Running --> Stopping : ordinary execution only: max_runtime deadline elapsed
Running --> Stopping : supervisor known absent; recovery exec.stop; outcome lost
Stopping --> Stopping : termination missing: repeat same E-stop\nunknown / contradictory: retain state and claim
Stopping --> Cleaning : stop / absence confirmed; record outcome\nordinary kept / standing idle; retirement only as authorised (§5.4)
Cleaning --> Cleaning : pending cleanup: same effect IDs\nunknown/refused identity revocation remains pending
Cleaning --> Terminal : applicable complete-content custody or per-act waiver; applicable cleanup confirmed (§§5.4, 7.1)
Terminal --> [*]
note right of Starting
  Owner: dispatcher service UID swarma-dispatcher.
  Daemon-owned supervisor, same UID.
  Launcher is root until exec under agent UID.
  R-LOCK: cancel before issue marks absent; launcher never called.
  After issue, mark in-flight cancel intent, resolve same receipt then stop.
  R-FATE: user-manager §7 owns unit/fate table; old daemon-instance writes fenced.
  Unknown start: wait for receipt/answer, never launch again.
  Exact failed-launch/pre-launch-cancel run-state edges are
  unspecified in spec §5.3; no extra stored state is invented.
end note
note left of Queued
  R-UNTRUSTED: slice 0/helper v0 refuse untrusted; no subscription binding/lease.
  R-CEILINGS/R-EXEC: matrix minimums and OS profile required.
  R-VERIFY: builds/tests on another machine only; no build job class here.
  Initial capacity closes -> refusal, no queued state.
  Quota / authority failures refuse in every slice, never queue.
  Cancel, window expiry (expired_in_queue), drain reject:
  exact run-state edges are unspecified in spec §§4.4, 9.
  No direct terminal edge bypassing cleanup is asserted.
end note
note right of Terminal
  R-OPERATOR: swarma-operator never hosts harness sessions; operator authority stays there.
  Signed operator records: operator device key on phone + biometric/content confirmation, or terminal password/content confirmation.
  Every operator act/record from agent sessions refuses; command/signature formats unpublished (§§3.2, 16).
  swarma-observer reads dispatcher state without confirmation; no mutation authority.
  R-STANDING: host loops trusted only; untrusted standing placement is workplace.
  R-WATCH v0/S0a: affected-account journaled stop, admission hold, observer status only.
  No per-account egress-freeze or phone-alert promise; v1/S2 lifecycle open (§§7.3, 16).
  R-ALLSTOP: direct cuts/stops; root start/create/ingress fence; unknown holds.
  Every service part including dispatcher reconciliation required before explicit recovery (§6).
  R-TRANSFER: separate physical materialize/work/export runs with own claims/receipts/stop/absence.
  Bounded original consent authorizes expiry export only; security holds stay closed; no helper retiring start.
  Fenced export: every blob/result durable outside deletion before discharge; workspace-transfer.puml.
  Refusal immutable; current-authority bounded repair uses new work/export effects; discard only per-act waiver.
  Retained content separately accounted until authenticated import acknowledgement/authorized release.
  Standing allocation exit does not retire it; operator-signed retirement only.
  Standing execution: no max_runtime quota or runtime deadline (§§3.5, 4.4).
  Sweep never stops it for runtime; applies in all backends.
  Ordinary execution: default 4 h, maximum 12 h; sweep stops at deadline (§7.2).
  R3 closed by owner decision 2026-10-12 (§16).
  Stored outcome is separate from run state:
  exit | failed | cancelled | expired | lost (§§4.4, 8.2).
  lost is an outcome, not a stored state.
  Exact terminal-state/outcome mapping is unspecified in spec §4.4.
  Host successor: lifecycle consent, same session/op replay -> same execution,
  previous claim absent, active owner ancestry and fresh start verdict; no reset ordinary budget.
  Host-requested stop recorded distinctly from owner cancel; no new outcome value.
  R-OUTCOME: pending E-stop continues identical arguments; terminal replay never signals.
  Stop scope is account-wide under latest-receipt fence, not session/time window.
  Dispatcher owns run records, claims, effects, receipts and logs;
  helper owns account ledger / termination evidence;
  launcher writes start receipt; broker owns bindings/leases.
  Agent and capacity claim lifecycles: agent-claim-states.puml.
end note
legend
  Defining spec: [[https://github.com/relux-works/swarma-dispatcher/blob/main/spec/dispatcher.md#44-execution-run1 §4.4 run/1]]
